    <!-- The recogniser refused to start at all, most often because the phone has no offline
         speech for its own language. Saying "Say again." here sends the crew round the same
         loop for ever, so say what happened and carry the detail. -->
    <string name="ask_recognition_failed">Speech recognition would not start: %1$s</string>
    <string name="ask_language_downloading">Getting the speech pack for this phone. Ask again in a moment.</string>
    <!-- The language the Ask feature listens and speaks in: a BCP 47 tag, and the language the
         phrases in ask_phrases and the answer wording are written in, not the phone's. Without it
         the recogniser follows the phone, which on a Finnish phone refuses outright
         (ERROR_LANGUAGE_NOT_SUPPORTED) and would never match these English words anyway, and the
         voice would read an English sentence with a Finnish mouth. A translator who translates
         ask_phrases translates this to match. -->
    <string name="ask_speech_language">en-US</string>
    <!-- What the whole crew hears: who asked, what they asked, and the answer, so an
